description:
Migrate component gold onto structured canonical entities after the instance and cardinality rulings.

Legacy shape:

- 481 `type:<taxonomy subtype>` cases are mechanically classifiable;
- 52 `third_party:<vendor>` cases assert vendor resolution;
- 30 `actor:user` cases wait on the taxonomy ruling;
- 53 duplicate repository/key groups cover 456 cases and require entity/evidence grouping rather than subtype collapse.

Migration assigns a stable repo-local gold entity id, asserted type/subtype, optional asserted vendor, and all supporting evidence. It preserves code/display names as candidates without requiring them as product identity.

Repeated subtype rows are grouped or kept distinct only from evidence-backed adjudication; never from arbitrary ordering. One known type-as-subtype label bug is corrected through its tracked bug.

Definition of done: every accepted component entity is canonical, same-subtype cardinality is preserved, and migration accounting covers every legacy component row.
